                    'en' => [
                        'soru' => 'Do you need ground preparation before installation?',
                        'cevap' => 'Yes—you need a flat, load-bearing, level base; concrete slab, compacted sand/gravel or a timber deck are options the survey evaluates. Example: for a 16 m² square unit the base is levelled to at least the footprint, drained, and left with access for anchor points. Alternative path: if the ground is sloping or loose, the crew recommends compaction, fill or a reinforced platform, with cost and time written into the quote. Source: survey → base note → install day flow plus product footprints. Is concrete mandatory? Not the only path, but stability is—choices happen on site. Field notes: /en/rehberler/bakim; quote and booking: /en/teklif-al; sizes: /en/urunler. Practice note: base acceptance criteria are levelness, load capacity and drainage; aesthetics are secondary. Slab thickness and anchor type are recommended in the survey report by unit size—we do not claim one fixed thickness. On compacted aggregate the sub-base is checked; on timber decks the minimum beam line is verified. Preparation work can be priced as a separate survey line item on the quote. Base acceptance scores level, load and drainage in the survey with pass / needs-fix / fail tags. Failed bases get a concrete slab or compacted aggregate recommendation; thickness is stated per unit size in the report—no single fixed number is claimed. Base work can be quoted as a separate line and moves the install date.',
                    ],
