                    'en' => [
                        'soru' => 'Should I choose a locally made gazebo or an imported one?',
                        'cevap' => 'Local production is preferred for 3 reasons — service response, spare-part supply and size changes move faster inside the same country, and the 5-year warranty applies either way. Alternative path: if a special profile colour or model only arrives from abroad, the import option is priced as its own line in the quote and the lead time is written clearly. Source: the production and logistics flow — install crew, warranty records and care visits sit in one system, and the 5-year warranty applies to both options. Pricing follows the same formula: area × language base rate × material × model × usage. The example 16 × 12,000 × 1.00 × 1.00 × 1.00 = TRY 192,000 sits inside the TRY 108,000–320,000 band; on an imported line any freight or currency difference appears as a separate row and is never hidden. Material multipliers (wood 1.00, composite 1.80, aluminium 2.50) and model multipliers (square 1.00, hex 1.20, modern 1.50) do not separate local from imported. Local builds can issue the technical sheet in Turkish and close tender document packs faster. Care advice still points to a 2–3 year recoat and an annual check. Practice note: the survey is free and runs Mon–Sat 09:00–18:00. Next step: browse local models on /urunler and ask for both local and import options side by side in your quote through /teklif-al. 1 logistics plan joins the quote: loading day, vehicle type and drop point. Local production keeps spare stock planned for 5 years. On an import line customs time appears as 1 row. Colour changes run faster on the local line. Warranty is 5 years either way.',
                    ],
